# Scoped byte-stability for byte-pinned assets (T5, design §4.13).
# These files are compared byte-for-byte by tests and rendered deterministically
# with LF line endings. eol=lf forces checkout with LF on every platform so a
# Windows/OneDrive host cannot drift a golden to CRLF (the failure mode found
# in the T5 recovery audit: content-identical "modified" golden in the worktree).
#
# Deliberately scoped: only the assets whose bytes are part of the contract.
# Everything else keeps git's default behavior.

*.service                 eol=lf
*.golden.*                eol=lf
internal/systemd/testdata/ eol=lf
internal/xray/testdata/    eol=lf
internal/origin/testdata/  eol=lf
